{
  "schema": "ralph-capability-contract/v2",
  "description": "Tracked contracts for capabilities that are declared in .factory/environment.toml and required by this product's conformance rows, plus candidate contracts for designed-but-unprovisioned capabilities. A declared capability without a contract, a contract without a passing non-skipped probe receipt, or a receipt that shows skip/simulated markers is unevidenced and is never auto-reclassified. A candidate contract is the committed probe definition for a capability that is not yet declared: the root endpoint refuses to run candidate contracts until the capability is declared, its contract is promoted to status=declared, and the runner class allowlist (root-configured, out-of-tree) grants it. The optional runner_class field records the dedicated runner class a probe is designed for (e.g. gpurunner, iprunner) so the intended class allowlist is explicit before provisioning. Probe argv is structural fail-closed: no contract may carry a fixture/simulation option token (--fixture, --fixture=, --fixture-dir, --fixture-facts), so a committed contract probe can never run in fixture mode, and receipts showing simulated fixture markers for declared contracts are rejected. Do not add contracts for unavailable capabilities with no designed probe.",
